      "created_at": "2018-02-16T12:04:20Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-02-16T12:04:20Z",
      "body": "I'm concerned that as the SaaS takes off, this will become a lot of work to hammer the Segment APIs. I'm assuming they won't rate-limit us, but if I'm to look into batching pings, or putting them into a local queue and having a pool of processes feeding them up to Segment, can I just confirm that it's OK if events are delayed sometimes (hours at worst) in the name of making the system more scaleable and fault-tolerant?",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
